 Animal Care Management Platform, Architecture & Technical Roadmap

> Status:
Proposed target architecture / evolving design document. This document describes the intended system,
not a claim that all components are implemented.

1. Purpose and scope

The Animal Care Management Platform is a Java-based project intended to help animal shelters and rescue organizations manage animal records, health and welfare, adoption, people, and daily operations in one place. Future releases may support veterinary clinics, farms, breeders, and other animal-care organizations.

Initial audience:** shelters and rescue groups. **Long-term direction:
configurable, 
multi-organization platform with appropriate access controls and data separation.

